{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2021-04-07 09:01:00', 'title': 'ABBVIE SUBMITS REGULATORY APPLICATIONS FOR SKYRIZI® (RISANKIZUMAB) IN PSORIATIC ARTHRITIS TO FDA AND EMA', 'text': 'NORTH CHICAGO, ILL., APRIL 7, 2021 /PRNEWSWIRE/ -- ABBVIE\xa0(NYSE: ABBV) TODAY ANNOUNCED THAT IT HAS SUBMITTED APPLICATIONS SEEKING APPROVAL FOR SKYRIZI® (RISANKIZUMAB-RZAA, 150 MG) TO THE U.S. FOOD AND DRUG ADMINISTRATION (FDA) AND FOR SKYRIZI® (RISANKIZUMAB, 150 MG) TO THE EUROPEAN MEDICINES AGENCY (EMA)\xa0FOR THE TREATMENT OF ADULTS WITH ACTIVE PSORIATIC ARTHRITIS.1\xa0THE SUBMISSIONS WERE SUPPORTED BY TWO PIVOTAL PHASE 3 STUDIES, KEEPSAKE-1 AND KEEPSAKE-2, WHICH EVALUATED SKYRIZI IN ADULTS WITH ACTIVE PSORIATIC ARTHRITIS INCLUDING THOSE WHO HAD RESPONDED INADEQUATELY OR WERE INTOLERANT TO BIOLOGIC THERAPY AND/OR NON-BIOLOGIC DISEASE-MODIFYING ANTI-RHEUMATIC DRUGS (DMARDS).1 "MOST PATIENTS LIVING WITH PSORIATIC ARTHRITIS EXPERIENCE BOTH SKIN AND JOINT DISEASE WHICH CAN BE ESPECIALLY BURDENSOME.'}